---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "18 June 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Network Notes — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Network Notes, the local-network messaging app for Mac by DataIsland Software LLC."
>

  <section class="legal fade-in">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/privacy">← All Privacy Policies</a></div>

    <h1>Network Notes — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">DataIsland Software LLC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      Network Notes is a local-network messaging app for macOS. This policy explains exactly
      what data Network Notes accesses, what leaves your device, and what is stored locally.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Network Notes collects no personal data and has no server.</strong> Messages
      travel directly between your Macs, encrypted end-to-end. Nothing passes through
      DataIsland or any third-party service. The app has no account, no analytics, and
      no internet requirement.
    </p>

    <h2>What Network Notes Accesses</h2>

    <h3>Local Network</h3>
    <p>
      Network Notes uses Bonjour (mDNS) to discover other Macs running Network Notes on
      your local network, and establishes direct peer-to-peer TCP connections to them.
      All communication is local — no traffic is routed to the internet.
    </p>

    <h3>Message Content</h3>
    <p>
      The text, images, and links you send are stored locally on your Mac in an encrypted
      SwiftData database. They are never transmitted to DataIsland or any external server.
      Message history is visible only on the Mac that sent or received them.
    </p>

    <h3>Display Name</h3>
    <p>
      Network Notes advertises your Mac's display name (defaulting to your Mac's computer
      name, which you can customise) to other Macs on the same network via Bonjour. This
      name is visible to anyone on the same local network who is running Network Notes.
      It is never sent to DataIsland or any internet service.
    </p>

    <h2>Encryption</h2>
    <p>
      Every message is encrypted end-to-end using AES-256-GCM. Encryption keys are derived
      via a P-256 Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman (ECDH) handshake that occurs directly between
      the two Macs. Your private key is generated on your device and stored only in your
      macOS Keychain. DataIsland never has access to your keys or your messages.
    </p>

    <h2>What Leaves Your Device</h2>
    <p>
      Network Notes makes no outgoing internet connections. The only data that leaves your
      Mac is the encrypted message payload sent directly to another Mac on the same local
      network. No data is sent to DataIsland or any third party.
    </p>

    <h2>Login Item</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to enable Open at Login, Network Notes registers itself as a login item
      using Apple's <code>SMAppService</code> API. This registration is stored locally by
      macOS and is not reported to DataIsland.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Message history is stored locally on your Mac for as long as you choose to keep it.
      You can delete individual messages or clear all history at any time from the history
      window. Deleting the app removes all locally stored data.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Network Notes does not collect any data from any user, including children. It has no
      account system, no analytics, and no network communication outside the local network.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially, the updated version will be posted at this URL with
      a new "Last updated" date. Because Network Notes collects no data, changes are expected
      to be minimal.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this privacy policy can be directed to
      <a href="mailto:support@dataisland.com">support@dataisland.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--blue); }
  .legal h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .legal h3 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.4rem; color: var(--blue); }
  .legal p  { font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--gray-dark); }
  .legal a  { color: var(--blue); }
  code { background: var(--gray-light); padding: 0.1em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
</style>
